-- Two elements side by side where an expression is one are one
-- unexpected_token at the second one's `<` and name (7:13 and 12:5),
-- saying that siblings need a fragment. After `</p>` or `/>` the `<` is a
-- comparison (language.md §11.2), but what the author wrote is a second
-- root, not markup passed as an argument.
sameLine =
    <p>a</p><p>b</p>


nextLine =
    <br />
    <hr />
